 "question": "Where does the game store the per-shot visual animation of the weapon model (the motion that continues while recoil is compensated, L4087), and what do optics and other parts do to it?",
 "sourceFacts": {
  "where": [
   "Each weapon blueprint (<Weapon>_WB) holds Class_76a3b0eb objects (three on 68 of 70 blueprints) whose member Field_f2d603de is a 59-member struct of per-shot animation settings. The blueprint entity lists two of them; a local replace-modifier (Class_8cdc5b63) installs the third.",
   "Member names come from Common/Gameplay/Soldier/Glacier_Soldier, object 52, member Field_60359d62: a binding struct with the same member hashes, each importing a named animation state (a732ab97 FB.Wep.Kickback.Amount, 1982d3c1 Kickback.Time, 2abd11c6 Pushback.Amount, 65f78a49 PitchKick.Amount, 0e7b114c RecoilSettle.Amplitude, f00a5d84 FB.CameraShake.Amplitude, 9aab20d7 Roll.Amplitude, 9923928e Yaw.Amplitude). 54 of 59 members are named this way; five are unbound.",
   "Multipliers sit in Class_bfd4f199 objects (215 across blueprints and part files; the registry's 'Proc Firing' annotations attach to this class only). Field_149939ab and Field_e9129d03 are the push and kick multipliers by annotation-value match ('60% Push/Kick' = 0.6 / 0.6); they are equal in all 215 objects, so which is which is not separable. Field_c4814c93 is a state selector (-1, 0 to 8) whose index meanings are not established."
  ],
