 "verification": "verify.py (main session) re-read the decoded files independently: 68 of 70 blueprints hold three settings objects (one holds 5, one 8); the AK205, QBZ192, Tavor7, M18 and CDX40 values match the trace; seven member hashes resolve through the Glacier_Soldier binding to the named animation states; 215 Class_bfd4f199 objects, none with unequal push and kick.",
 "inference": [
  "The weapon model's push, kick, pitch kick, roll, yaw, settle and a camera shake are a separate, per-weapon animation layer with its own optic multipliers. It is the layer seen moving under compensation in the L4087 clips.",
  "WPM_Procedural_GlobalScaling_Primary (0.88 on selector -1, 0.6 on selector 0) is imported by every primary blueprint checked, so a global visual-kick scale applies before any optic.",
  "The SU-230 (WPM_SCP_ElcanDR) push/kick multiplier went from 1.0005 on 1.4.3.5 to 0.55 on 2.1.1.0, the update whose notes say the scope 'no longer incorrectly reduces visual recoil'. The earlier L4071 reading tied that note to the camera-recoil override file; this multiplier changed in the same update."
 ],
